replies.text:
@mattmorrow7777 Winters can be brutal.  I have flown into Billings many times to visit friends living in the Cody area.  When he picked me up at the airport he told me to cover my mouth and not to breath in the air as it could freeze my lungs.  I had never experienced 50 below with the wind chill.  But I still love that region.  

My favorite time of year is in the spring when the animals are birthing their young and in the fall when the leaves change.....not as many tourists since the kids are back in school.  

You should visit Thermopolis next time you go then do the drive across the Big Horns to NE Wyoming....its awesome!
